{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "025L", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$A$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$f : A \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$A$", "MATH_0005": "$B$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{proposition-etale-regular}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proposition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f76005b893a42508210a24175c4d999fb045694ee7446e705bb74389896d94ac", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e9d9546373ec4d06d47d0655a35fb0a1b2032565343f3c5ca305426fb14a70ed", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be Noetherian local rings.\nLet <MATH_0003> be an <ACCENT_0001>tale homomorphism of local rings.\nThen <MATH_0004> is regular if and only if <MATH_0005> is so.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7a031f4330cc0da2ebdda17cb48d7ef2182e7a3a4066c7741ddac437952e74ee", "unit_id": "tag:025N:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "025L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathfrak m$", "MATH_0005": "$A$", "MATH_0006": "$\\dim_{\\kappa(\\mathfrak m)} \\mathfrak m/\\mathfrak m^2 =\n\\dim(A) = \\dim(B)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathfrak mB$", "MATH_0008": "$B$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathfrak m_B/\\mathfrak m_B = \\mathfrak mB/\\mathfrak m^2B$", "MATH_0010": "$\\dim(B)$", "MATH_0011": "$B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-flat-under-regular}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-etale-dimension}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-flat-over-regular-with-regular-fibre}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a24966f8aa526c6940701ece71f4cadcf3523a17acb37eb965bf497ff1def8d1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b1fdb6e63f355ae43cd9949282d3f50f1e4f09e443dc8260cf852afdb7821f8b", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is regular, then <MATH_0002> is regular by\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nAssume <MATH_0003> is regular. Let <MATH_0004> be the maximal ideal\nof <MATH_0005>. Then <MATH_0006> (see Lemma <REF_0002>).\nOn the other hand, <MATH_0007> is the maximal ideal of\n<MATH_0008> and hence <MATH_0009>\nis generated by at most <MATH_0010> elements. Thus <MATH_0011> is regular.\n(You can also use the slightly more general\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>.)\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:edc2d90ae7fcf71918220181fa257581d212204881d617499618e2dfdcddda33", "unit_id": "tag:025N:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "025L", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$A$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$f : A \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$A$", "MATH_0005": "$B$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{proposition-etale-reduced}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proposition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f76005b893a42508210a24175c4d999fb045694ee7446e705bb74389896d94ac", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4ef6a2c80c12c5e84ca0992b438169b5fe16df75937f51fc232adfd17e98eb06", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be Noetherian local rings.\nLet <MATH_0003> be an <ACCENT_0001>tale homomorphism of local rings.\nThen <MATH_0004> is reduced if and only if <MATH_0005> is so.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d5cebcf0413456075402f0b7b438970c438bb6b3f42cb5d214e252f8470feec2", "unit_id": "tag:025O:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "025L", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "MATH_0004": "$A$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$A$", "MATH_0007": "$B'$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0009": "$B'$", "MATH_0010": "$B'$", "MATH_0011": "$A$", "MATH_0012": "$A \\to B'$", "MATH_0013": "$B'$", "MATH_0014": "$B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-descent-reduced}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-etale-Noetherian}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-reduced-goes-up}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:17c522901dfc85adcc1dd11dcaf63a3e690d52a096515e36e73c8084cb84c029", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:af0e4e59cd03033180b09a24025b7a8e60abb868ef84f08fb8ed0ecf4736809b", "source_text": "It is clear from the faithful flatness of <MATH_0001> that if <MATH_0002> is reduced, so\nis <MATH_0003>. See also Algebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nConversely, assume <MATH_0004> is reduced. By assumption <MATH_0005> is a localization\nof a finite type <MATH_0006>-algebra <MATH_0007> at some prime <MATH_0008>.\nAfter replacing <MATH_0009> by a localization we may assume that <MATH_0010>\nis <ACCENT_0001>tale over <MATH_0011>, see Lemma <REF_0002>.\nThen we see that Algebra, Lemma <REF_0003> applies to\n<MATH_0012> and <MATH_0013> is reduced. Hence <MATH_0014> is reduced.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a3a0ae9bf055437b86b6f3aa6051093069e52053df6983825f09d316a19c03ae", "unit_id": "tag:025O:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "025L", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "MATH_0004": "$A$", "MATH_0005": "$A^\\wedge$", "MATH_0006": "$A \\to A^\\wedge$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathfrak m_AA^\\wedge$", "MATH_0008": "$A^\\wedge$", "MATH_0009": "$A$", "MATH_0010": "$A^\\wedge$", "MATH_0011": "$A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{examples-section-local-completion-nonreduced}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-technicality-needed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:454347da6ed9a74f78389f038dde1dc35209224c2b541d08850f75dc913862cc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6bea3741b81967c9c36b129c4e6ec4e58d635314d3413902643a5c7a4bc47867", "source_text": "The result on ``reducedness'' does not hold with a weaker\ndefinition of <ACCENT_0001>tale local ring maps <MATH_0001> where one\ndrops the assumption that <MATH_0002> is essentially of finite type over <MATH_0003>.\nNamely, it can happen that a Noetherian local domain <MATH_0004> has nonreduced\ncompletion <MATH_0005>, see\nExamples, Section <REF_0001>.\nBut the ring map <MATH_0006> is flat, and <MATH_0007>\nis the maximal ideal of <MATH_0008> and of course <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010> have\nthe same residue fields. This is why it is important to consider\nthis notion only for ring extensions which are essentially of finite type\n(or essentially of finite presentation if <MATH_0011> is not Noetherian).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:700e33bd7f0a346c05856067b7b1f3474ce3f01df455006b7ce2038bf487ab15", "unit_id": "tag:039U:statement"}
